{
  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_001: multimodal, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → 58.6% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over the image modality alone. config_025 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer) keeps the image encoder and aggregation identical to config_001, isolating the contribution of the RNA modality and the fusion step. If image-only approaches or exceeds 58.6%, the RNA branch is not helping and subsequent experiments should focus on image architecture and aggregation; if it falls well below, multimodal fusion is confirmed as beneficial and we should optimize the RNA encoder and fusion strategy. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design choice (whether to invest in multimodal vs. image-focused configurations) and will guide all 7 remaining experiments."
}

